14:overrides, brand-on-brand contrast, a `ThemeProvider` that themes the whole page, the
88:Hue families: `black`, `white`, `blue`, `green`, `yellow`, `orange`, `red`, `purple`,
105:| `--g-color-base-*`                                | Backgrounds & fills             | `base-background`, `base-brand`, `base-generic`, `base-danger-medium`    |
106:| `--g-color-text-*`                                | Text colors                     | `text-primary`, `text-secondary`, `text-hint`, `text-brand`, `text-link` |
107:| `--g-color-line-*`                                | Borders, dividers, underlines   | `line-generic`, `line-brand`, `line-focus`, `line-danger`                |
114:  `utility` (purple), `misc` (cool grey), plus `brand`, `generic` and `neutral`.
118:  (e.g. `base-brand` / `base-brand-hover`).
134:### Accent / brand color
136:The accent color is what makes an app feel branded — action buttons, active controls, links, and
141:| `--g-color-base-brand`              | Brand background (action button, active controls) |
142:| `--g-color-base-brand-hover`        | Hover background                                  |
143:| `--g-color-base-selection`          | Lighter brand tint (List/Table row selection)     |
145:| `--g-color-line-brand`              | Brand lines (active tab underline)                |
146:| `--g-color-text-brand`              | Brand text                                        |
147:| `--g-color-text-brand-heavy`        | Brand text over a background                      |
148:| `--g-color-text-brand-contrast`     | Text placed **on top of** a brand background      |
156:  --g-color-base-brand: rgb(117, 155, 255);
157:  --g-color-base-brand-hover: rgb(99, 143, 255);
160:  --g-color-line-brand: rgb(117, 155, 255);
161:  --g-color-text-brand: rgb(117, 155, 255);
162:  --g-color-text-brand-contrast: rgb(255, 255, 255);
168:> Set these on the theme class (e.g. `.g-root_theme_light`) if the brand color should differ
229:respects any brand overrides — no conditional theme logic in your components.
243:  --g-color-base-brand: rgb(117, 155, 255);
254:### Rebranding: do it completely
256:> **Don't override just 2–4 tokens.** If you only set `--g-color-base-brand`, then selection,
258:> mismatched. Override the **full brand token set** (the [accent table](#accent--brand-color)
260:> brighter brand color than light).
